  "repair": "All three diagnostic model runners register their current process with the invoking native/browser workflow. The executor finish hook cancels and joins that process even when the bounded planner has already delivered cancellation. Production planner early-cancellation and late-proposal rejection semantics are unchanged.",
  "validation": [
    "The first shell fixture incorrectly used positional arguments inside its cleanup function; its first red/green attempts cannot isolate process-join timing. Both failures remain recorded.",
    "After correcting the marker path, the original no-finish-hook boundary fails the immediate cleanup assertion while eventual cleanup passes. Joining in finishRun passes, together with two existing native cancellation regressions.",
    "The native form workflow passes a 20-second no-inference delay before completion, with exact Unicode, same field UUID/value/selection, simulated login/Resume, five verified dispatches and no replay. Only two unrelated destruction notifications were observed.",
    "The actual Fara Q4 task reaches its 90-second cancellation deadline. The task report now records ownedWorkerExited=true at return. All six individual probe reports confirm process exit and credential removal; the last is a cancelled diagnostic."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "Fara repeatedly proposes y=622, which points to the Destination label rather than the native editable row. It performs one Tab key action; the native multiline Origin editor inserts a literal tab, retains focus, and the final independent state is Origin=\\t and Destination empty. This is a failed natural-language task.",
    "Native key delivery is literal; do not globally block Tab or rewrite it to focus traversal. The model needs bounded exact editable-state observations, including whitespace/selection and explicit truncation, to understand these effects. Preserve secure-field exclusion and avoid guessing target coordinates.",
    "Offline comparison of retained Holo trial04 fixture crops shows one connected changed region: 838 pixels at crop bounds [0,144,30,175], with maximum channel difference 216, around the Grammarly overlay near Origin. The completion revalidation also observed a caret-region difference. This does not justify ignoring arbitrary visible content.",
    "The no-inference delay control passes and therefore does not establish inference latency alone as the cause of the remaining Holo completion mismatch."
  ],
